OL,3,GNEWSA'Gambling controlled me,' says
OL,4,Aformer footballer
OL,5,
OL,6,FFormer Stoke City footballer Tony Kelly
OL,7,Fhas described how gambling took over
OL,8,Fhis life, with rising debts and family
OL,9,Fbreakdowns contributing to problems on
OL,10,Fthe pitch.
OL,12,FHe said he had lost more than #500,000
OL,13,Fto gambling after what started as "a
OL,14,Fbit of fun".
OL,16,FKelly, who grew up in Coventry, spent
OL,17,Fthree years at Stoke where he enjoyed
OL,18,Fsome of the biggest moments of his
OL,19,Ffootball career, including winning the
OL,20,FFootball League Trophy in 1992 and
OL,21,Fscoring an equaliser against Liverpool
OL,22,Fin the League Cup in 1991.
OL,23,APub: 25-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
